│ patch_description        │ The key innovation is the use of local rolling normalization (Z-scaling and Percentile    │
│                          │ Ranking) for every core feature to ensure regime-invariance. The primary obstacle in the  │
│                          │ previous version was the collapse of the predictive slope (0.07 train vs 0.006 val),      │
│                          │ indicating that the model's absolute-value features (like raw returns or volatility) lost │
│                          │ their meaning across market regime shifts.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By replacing raw returns with returns scaled by local idiosyncratic volatility (Z-scores) │
│                          │ and raw indicators with rolling percentile ranks (e.g., volume rank, candle-range rank),  │
│                          │ the model identifies relative patterns that are statistically identical whether BTC is at │
│                          │ $20k or $60k, or whether local volatility is 0.5% or 5.0%. I also increased               │
│                          │ `min_child_weight` and added L2 regularization (`reg_lambda`) to the XGBoost parameters   │
│                          │ to prevent overfitting to regime-specific noise and force a more substantial predictive   │
│                          │ slope.                                                                                    │
