│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ regime_short_xgb                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current model uses moderately deep trees, weak regularization, and many long-horizon  │
│                          │ features (20–200 bar windows) that fit the training regime too tightly. That explains the │
│                          │ sharp train→val slope collapse and the low prediction variance on validation.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This rewrite changes the internal algorithm in three ways:                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Shorter, more regime-invariant features:                                               │
│                          │    - Uses mostly 3–20 bar windows instead of 60+ bar windows.                             │
│                          │    - Adds rolling z-scores for returns, volatility, volume, and range so the model sees   │
│                          │ normalized deviations rather than raw levels.                                             │
│                          │    - Adds “trend of regime” features like volatility trend, efficiency trend, and         │
│                          │ autocorrelation trend to capture changing market character.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Explicit feature interactions that generalize:                                         │
│                          │    - Momentum × volatility-regime                                                         │
│                          │    - Momentum × efficiency                                                                │
│                          │    - Volume pressure × volatility regime                                                  │
│                          │    These interactions are more stable than using the raw components alone.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. Better XGBoost bias/variance control:                                                  │
│                          │    - Shallower trees with more samples per leaf                                           │
│                          │    - Stronger L1/L2 regularization                                                        │
│                          │    - Slightly lower learning rate with more estimators                                    │
│                          │    - Early stopping on the test split remains unchanged by interface, but the model is    │
│                          │ less likely to overfit the train regime                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I also reduce target clipping slightly and lower the minimum acceptable prediction std    │
│                          │ ratio so the model is less aggressively flattened. The goal is to restore validation      │
│                          │ slope and prediction spread without exceeding the train→val generalization gap.           │
