│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the core failure mode: the model’s slope collapses out-of-sample        │
│                          │ because many current features are too level-dependent and too slow-moving. I’m replacing  │
│                          │ the long-horizon, regime-specific feature set with a more compact, shorter-memory set     │
│                          │ that is normalized within rolling windows, so the same pattern means roughly the same     │
│                          │ thing across volatility regimes.                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Use shorter lookbacks for returns, volatility, RSI, ATR, MACD, and volume ratios.       │
│                          │ - Add rolling z-score normalization for price, returns, volatility, ATR, and volume so    │
│                          │ the model sees standardized deviations rather than raw levels.                            │
│                          │ - Add regime-change features such as volatility trend and efficiency trend, which are     │
│                          │ more transferable across shifts than absolute regime levels.                              │
│                          │ - Keep the useful momentum × volatility interaction, but make it based on short-horizon   │
│                          │ normalized signals.                                                                       │
│                          │ - Remove some long-window, redundant features that likely overfit the training regime.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I also tighten XGBoost to reduce memorization: fewer trees, slightly shallower depth,     │
│                          │ stronger regularization, and higher min_child_weight. This should reduce train/val slope  │
│                          │ collapse while keeping enough expressivity to improve val_DA and val_slope.               │
