│ patch_name               │ robust_short_regime_features                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ This edit aims to solve the slope collapse by making the feature set more                 │
│                          │ regime-invariant and more responsive to recent market structure. It does three things:    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Shortens the effective lookback horizon** for core momentum/volatility signals so    │
│                          │ they decay faster and are less tied to stale training regimes.                            │
│                          │ 2. **Adds rolling z-score normalization and trend-of-regime features** for volatility,    │
│                          │ autocorrelation, and efficiency ratio, which helps the model compare “recent” behavior    │
│                          │ relative to the local past instead of using absolute levels.                              │
│                          │ 3. **Relaxes model regularization slightly** and increases tree count a bit so XGBoost    │
│                          │ can recover predictive slope without collapsing predictions toward the mean.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The feature count remains well under the 80-feature limit, and all features use only past │
│                          │ data.                                                                                     │
