│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the main failure mode: the model’s slope collapses in the newest        │
│                          │ regime, which usually means it is learning absolute levels that do not survive regime     │
│                          │ shifts. The proposed feature set emphasizes short-horizon, regime-invariant signals:      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - shorter lookbacks for returns, volatility, trend strength, and mean-reversion           │
│                          │ - rolling z-scored versions of return, volatility, RSI, and price deviation               │
│                          │ - explicit rate-of-change features for volatility and efficiency                          │
│                          │ - short-window autocorrelation and its trend, which helps capture market character        │
│                          │ changes                                                                                   │
│                          │ - a stronger momentum × volatility-regime interaction using normalized momentum           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I also slightly relax the tree regularization so XGBoost can fit these more informative   │
│                          │ but noisier short-term signals without collapsing toward the mean. This should help raise │
│                          │ val_slope and pred_std_ratio while keeping overfit under control.                         │
