│ patch_description        │ This version switches to a regime-invariant, micro-regime feature bank rather than        │
│                          │ long-horizon technical indicators.                                                        │
│                          │ The core idea is to convert price, volatility, volume, and funding into short-window      │
│                          │ standardized signals, then add rate-of-change and interaction terms so the trees can      │
│                          │ learn when a pattern is strengthening or weakening across regimes.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should work better:                                                              │
│                          │ - It avoids relying on absolute levels that tend to break under regime shifts.            │
│                          │ - It emphasizes short lookbacks (5–20 bars) and rolling z-scores/ranks, which are more    │
│                          │ stable across changing volatility.                                                        │
│                          │ - It adds trend-of-regime features like volatility momentum, efficiency momentum, and     │
│                          │ spread between fast/slow normalized signals.                                              │
│                          │ - It keeps the model compact but expressive, with enough trees to learn nonlinear         │
│                          │ interactions without over-regularizing into mean predictions.                             │
